\tag{fdip}
\title{Two-valued invariants at self-opposite labels}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{When two spectral subspaces carry opposite translation labels, a symmetry can exchange them. At a label equal to its opposite, the same symmetry acts inside one subspace. Which constraints on multiplicities and signs can be read from those labels alone?}

\p{The [translation blocks](fdip-016C) are taken for a finite periodic grid with positive periods. Real alternating forms use the [Pfaffian element and its volume](fdip-008I). A complex spectral subspace and a real space carrying a skew form supply different sign data.}

